Subject: [PATCH] Introduce 'edge' signature design language and apply it to
 the Home hero
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per the design-lead approach: ground the visual signature in the
brand name itself rather than a generic dark-mode-with-glow default.
'Edges Enterprise' -> a chamfered top-right corner motif ('the edge')
used consistently on cards, panels, and primary buttons.

- index.css: .edge-cut / .edge-cut-sm / .edge-cut-lg clip-path
  utilities (chamfer size scales via --edge-cut), .edge-divider
  gradient rule for between-section breaks
- New src/components/motion/EdgeCard.js: chamfered card with a
  hairline border and a soft brand-color glow that intensifies on
  hover, built on Framer Motion
- New src/components/motion/AmbientGlow.js: decorative pulsing
  gradient blobs for hero backgrounds — aria-hidden, and holds still
  under prefers-reduced-motion
- Reveal.js now also respects prefers-reduced-motion (skips the
  slide, keeps a quick fade) as a11y quality-floor
- Home.js: stat blocks become EdgeCards, hero gets an AmbientGlow
  layer, an edge-divider separates the stats from the next section,
  and the 'Learn More' button picks up the chamfer + brand glow

Scoped to the Home hero for now — same components are ready to reuse
across Services/About/Products/Contact in a follow-up pass.
